<title>BELGIUM: EU'S VAN MIERT SILENT ON KESKO/TUKO MERGER.</title>
<headline>EU'S VAN MIERT SILENT ON KESKO/TUKO MERGER.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union Competition Commissioner Karel Van Miert declined on Wednesday to comment on whether the Commission would approve the merger of Finnish wholesalers Kesko and Tuko.</p>
<p>&quot;It is too early (to say anything)...discussions are going on, it is all I can say,&quot; he told Reuters.</p>
<p>An EU source said last week the Commission would only clear Kesko's acquisition of Tuko if changes are made to the deal.</p>
<p>The Commission, which vets mergers and other corporate deals to see whether they may harm competition in the 15-nation bloc, fears the deal will lead to a dominant market position.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
</text>
